following scenarios:
◦ Procedural continuous assign statements.
◦ LHS of Non blocking assignment statements.
◦ $monitor statements.
• Limited debug support. Only UCLI show/get value is supported.
Pattern Matching for Tagged Union
VCS supports the pattern matching of tagged union expressions in if-else conditional
statements, case statements as specified in the Section 12.6 of the IEEE Standard
System Verilog LRM 1800-2012.
The following examples shows the usage of pattern matching.
Example 54 Usage of Pattern Matching for Tagged Union in if-else Conditional Statement
typedef union tagged packed {
int Valid;
struct packed {
bit [4:0] reg1, reg2, regd;
} Add;
} Instr;

module test;
Instr i1;
int v;

Pattern Matching for Tagged Union
i1 = tagged Valid(100);
if (i1 matches tagged Valid) begin
$display(i1.Valid);
end
end
Example 55 Usage of Pattern Matching for Tagged Union in Case Statement
typedef union tagged packed
{
void Invalid;
int Valid;
} Vint;

module test;
Vint v;
v = tagged Valid 32'd12;
case (v) matches
tagged Invalid : $display("v is Invalid");
tagged Valid : $display("v is Valid with value=%0d", v.Valid);
endcase
end
