User-Defined Payload
The use-model to establish the communication with user-defined payload between SV
VMM and SC TLM2.0 is same as explained in the sections. The only difference is that
for user-defined payloads, SC has to provide pack/unpack functions for the following two
functions and should compile and link these functions.
void tli_conv2_pack_tlmgp (tli_pack_data& P, T& gp) ;
//T - user defined payload type

void tli_conv2_unpack_tlmgp (tli_pack_data& P, T& gp);
For the generic payload type, VCS TLI adapters provide the implementation of the earlier
mentioned functions and therefore, it is not required to be implemented again.
To ease the pack or unpack implementation, VCS TLI adapters introduced the pack or
unpack operators and methods based on the data type of each field in the payload class.
For more information, refer to Exchanging Data Between SystemVerilog and SystemC
Using Byte Pack/Unpack.

3. The USER_PAYLOAD define needs to be used while compiling the SC file which includes
tli_sc_bindings.h.
