Support for TLI Adapter in a Package
The TLI adapter code can also be created in the form of an SV package.
To create the code in a package, create a create_as_package directive in the TLI file.
The TLI file is provided with the SystemC module to the syscan call.
The SV package generated from the TLI file is tli_<scmodule_name> and the syntax of
the created SV tasks/functions is <scmodule_name>_<SC_method_name>.
Set the scope of the SystemC instance with the Verilog function as follows:
scSetScopeByName("<systemc_scope_path>");
The maximum number of concurrent task calls can also be changed in the TLI file by
providing the value with the MAX_TASK_CALLS <new_value> directive.

Support for TLI Adapter in a Package
new_value is the value provided for the number of concurrent tasks. By default, the value
is 100.
