Support for Select of Virtual Interface XMR Connected to
Task/Function Ref Port
VCS supports connecting a select of a virtual interface cross-module reference (XMR) to
a task or function ref port. A virtual interface XMR refers to any member of an interface
accessed through a virtual interface typed node. When the select expression includes
an interface array index and the base of the select is such a virtual interface XMR, VCS
compiles and simulates the connection correctly. Value changes made through the ref
port propagate to sensitivity and event controls on the connected target, and vice versa.
Previously NYI-failing patterns now compile and run. Legal ref-port connections that
already compiled are unchanged.
% vcs -sverilog <file_name>
Example 112 Value Change in Task; Dynamic Event Outside Task
interface simple_if;
logic valid[2];

task automatic touch_task(ref logic valid);
valid = 1'b1;

module tb_top;
simple_if phy_if();
virtual simple_if virt_inst[2];

cls c = new;
phy_if.valid[0] = 1'b0;
virt_inst[0] = phy_if;
c.touch_task(tb_top.virt_inst[0].valid[0]);
end
always @(virt_inst[0].valid[0]) begin
end
assert(count == 1) $display ("Passed!");

else $display ("Failed!");
end
No compile-time error.
Runtime result:
Passed!
Example 113 Value Change Outside Task; Dynamic Event Inside Task
