The following limitations must be noted while using the -xlrm
uniq_prior_final option for loop indices:
• It must be written in for statement. The while and dowhile are not supported.
• The loop bounds must be the compile-time constants.
• for(i= lsb; i<msb; i++)
• Here, lsb and msb must be compile-time constant, or becomes constant when upper
loops get unrolled.
• No other drivers of the loop variable must be in the loop body.
VCS also supports unique/prior final in a for loop that cannot be unrolled at compile
time. For example, you might have a for loop whose range cannot be determined at
compile time. If there are errors during the last evaluation of such a for loop, VCS still
reports the error. However, loop index information is not provided. Even if multiple failures
occur in different iterations, VCS reports only the last one.
