System Tasks to Control Warning Messages
Two system tasks $uniq_prior_checkon and $uniq_prior_checkoff enable you to
switch on/off runtime warning messages for unique/priority if/case statements. The
following example illustrates the use model of these tasks to ignore violations:
Example 124 System tasks to control warning messages
//test.sv
bit sel, v1, v2;

//Disable this initial block to display all RT warning messages
$display($time, " Priority checker OFF\n");
$uniq_prior_checkoff();
#1;
$display($time, " Priority checker ON\n");
$uniq_prior_checkon();
end

//violation with this set of values (warning disabled)
sel = 1'b1;
v1 = 1'b1;
v2 = 1'b1;
#1;
//violation with this set of values (warning enabled)
sel = 1'b0;
v1 = 1'b0;
v2 = 1'b0;
#1;
end
unique case(sel)
v1: $display($time, " Hello");
