Support for Object Handle Comparison in Constraint Guards
In Example 168, a different constraint is applied to the variable x depending on the object
handles a1 and a3. If a1 equals to a3, x is constrained to 3. If a1 is not equal to a3, x is
constrained to 5. The following is the result of the example:
