Support for default :/ expression in SystemVerilog dist Constraints
Semantics
• Default range definition: The default term denotes all values of the distribution
expression’s self‑determined type that are not covered by any other explicit
dist_item.
• Operator restriction: The default item must use :/; := or omission of :/ is illegal and
reported as an error.
• Uniqueness: At most one default specification may appear in a distribution.
• Normalization model: During elaboration, VCS conceptually models default as the
complement of all explicit ranges. For example:
rand unsigned int x; // [0 : 2^32-1]
x dist { [100:102] := 1, default :/ 1 };
// Modeled as:
x dist { [100:102] := 1, { [0:99], [103:2^32-1] } :/ 1 };
Supported Cases and Examples
Basic
class inner;
rand int unsigned x; // [0 : 2^32-1] by definition
constraint cons { x dist { [100:102] := 1, default :/ 2 }; }
Default position variations
x dist { [10:102] := 1, default :/ 2, [200:300] := 3 };
x dist { default :/ 2, [200:300] := 3, [10:102] := 1 };
Under guard and function guard constraint modes
b == 0 -> x dist { default :/ 2, [10:102] := 1 };
get_b() -> x dist { default :/ 2, [10:102] := 1 };
Default in multiple dists
x dist { default :/ 2, [10:102] := 1 };
x dist { default :/ 20, [1:202] := 2 };
x dist { default :/ 100, [100:402] := 3 };
Multiple variable weights in multiple dists and std::randomize
// Variable-based weights
x dist { default :/ b, [10:102] := 1 };
x dist { default :/ c, [1:202] := 2 };
x dist { default :/ d, [100:402] := 3 };

Support for Typecast in Constraints
// Multiple Variable-based weights
x dist {default :/ (b + c + d), [10:102] := 1};
x dist {default :/ c, [1:202] := 2};
x dist {default :/ d, [100:402] := 3};
// std::randomize with expressions
std::randomize(k) with {
k.x dist { default :/ (k.b + k.c + k.d), [10:102] := 1 };
k.x dist { default :/ k.c, [1:202] := 2 };
k.x dist { default :/ k.d, [100:402] := 3 };
};
Enums and packed structs
// Enums
rspOpc dist { E1 :/ 1, E2 := 3, default :/ 1 };
rspRdwAlign dist {E1 :/ 1, E2 := ww1, default :/ 3};
Packed struct slicing in foreach
foreach (st[i]) begin
st[i][3:2] dist { [1:3] := 10, [2:4] := 5, default :/ 1 };
end
Arrays with foreach and variable weights
foreach (arr[i]) {
arr[i] dist { default :/ (b + c + d), [10:102] := 1 };
arr[i] dist { default :/ c, [1:202] := 2 };
arr[i] dist { default :/ d, [100:402] := 3 };
}
• Variables inside interval bounds combined with default: Intervals such as [100:b]
with a default item are not supported. In this case, VCS issues the Error-[NYI-
CSTR-DIST-DEF-NON-CONST] error message at compile time.
• Floating-point intervals and weights are not supported in the default dist item. In this
case, VCS issues the Error-[CSTR-DIST-DEF-NON-INT] error message at compile
• Specifying a default with := is not supported. In this case, VCS issues the Error-
[CNST-DIST-DEF] error message at compile time.
Support for Typecast in Constraints
You can use a cast ( ' ) operator on constraints as defined in the IEEE SystemVerilog
LRM Std 1800™-2012 Section 6.24, “Casting”.

Support for Typecast in Constraints
The following is the syntax for casting constraints.
constant_cast ::= casting_type ' ( constant_expression )
cast ::= casting_type ' ( expression )
casting_type ::= simple_type | constant_primary | signing
simple_type ::= integer_type | ps_type_identifier |
ps_parameter_identifier
integer_type::= bit | logic | reg | byte | shortint | int | longint |
