Arguments
VCS supports the randomization of dynamic MDA elements specified in the
arguments of the randomized calls. That is, for randomize calls std::randomize() or
obj.randomize() with an array type variable, VCS considers the variable and its array
elements as random variables. For example, if the randomize call std::randomize(xvar)
is used as follows:
int xvar[][4];
endclass;
